align-table-center"><caption><strong>Alum Rock Union Elementary School District</strong><br><strong>Measure P</strong><br><strong>General Obligation Bond</strong><br><strong>55% Vote Required</strong></caption><tbody><tr><td>With funds that cannot be taken by the State or Federal government, shall Alum Rock Union Elementary School District's measure to repair leaky roofs and plumbing; replace heating, ventilation, and air conditioning; and upgrade emergency communication and security systems be adopted, authorizing $100 million of bonds with legal rates, without increasing current tax rates, average levies below $26 per $100,000 of assessed valuation (raising $6.3 million annually while outstanding), audits, independent oversight, and disclosure of all spending?</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td><strong>YES</strong><br><strong>NO</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p><a href="https://files.santaclaracounty.gov/exjcpb1296/2026-08/measure-p_alum-rock-union-general-obligation-bond-primary-argument-in-favor_redacted_final.pdf?VersionId=QbWWz2plqZ1L.wCd0aeLDUsfGmQXJnVX" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="99851a02-0632-4dfb-b3fc-34b2543c6f19" data-entity-substitution="media" title="Measure P_Alum Rock Union General Obligation Bond_ Primary Argument in Favor_Redacted_Final"><strong>Primary Argument In-Favor</strong></a>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Primary Argument Against</strong><em> (none filed)</em></p><p><a href="https://files.santaclaracounty.gov/exjcpb1296/2026-08/alum-rock-union-esd-bond-measure-ia-nov-26-to-rov-final_redacted.pdf?VersionId=wHC3Gme81VWm0wm_ZojVC4k1MGKwVRah" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="c6600201-6af7-412e-a2e4-6b98b78efbb6" data-entity-substitution="media" title="Alum Rock Union ESD Bond Measure IA - Nov 26 (to ROV)_Final_Redacted"><strong>Impartial Analysis</strong></a></p><hr><table class="align-table-left align-table-center"><caption><strong>Cambrian School District</strong><br><strong>Measure Q</strong><br><strong>Parcel Tax</strong><br><strong>2/3rds (66.67%) Vote Required</strong></caption><tbody><tr><td>To protect the quality of education in our local elementary and middle schools, provide funding for core academic programs in math, science, engineering, technology, reading, writing and arts, attract/retain highly qualified teachers, and maintain manageable class sizes, shall Cambrian School District's measure be adopted, levying $148/parcel for 8 years, its continuance subject to voter approval, with senior exemptions, annual inflation adjustments, providing $1,000,000 annually in locally controlled funding that can't be taken by the State?</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td><strong>YES</strong><br><strong>NO</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p><a href="https://files.santaclaracounty.gov/exjcpb1296/2026-08/measure-q_cambrian-school-district-parcel-tax_primary-argument-in-favor_redacted_final.pdf?VersionId=9c2QO2Ij25_Kv2uvoDRPmN.R31yvMeL0" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="dffec1a6-7f01-44c0-8824-8631f529e12c" data-entity-substitution="media" title="Measure Q_Cambrian School District Parcel Tax_Primary Argument in Favor_Redacted_Final"><strong>Primary Argument In-Favor</strong></a>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Primary Argument Against</strong><em> (none filed)</em></p><p><a href="https://files.santaclaracounty.gov/exjcpb1296/2026-08/alum-rock-union-esd-bond-measure-ia-nov-26-to-rov-final_redacted_0.pdf?VersionId=ZsZUMDSKQkFXnw4fPoV.JdbIOS2SSaVb" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="4e54c401-1c7d-4dad-bdd5-bbd39b6f2137" data-entity-substitution="media" title="Cambrian SD Parcel Tax IA - Nov 26 (to ROV)_Final_Redacted"><strong>Impartial Analysis</strong></a></p><hr><table class="align-table-left align-table-center"><caption><strong>Orchard School District</strong><br><strong>Measure R</strong><br><strong>Parcel Tax</strong><br><strong>2/3rds (66.67%) Vote Required</strong></caption><tbody><tr><td>To enhance and create quality educational opportunities, attract and retain teachers and staff, support Science, Technology, Engineering, Arts and Mathematics (STEAM) education and visual and performing arts, shall the Orchard School District measure levying a parcel tax at the rate of 4 cents per building square foot (not-to-exceed $7,500 non-residential and $89 residential per parcel), raising $1.4 million annually for eight years beginning July 1, 2027, with senior exemptions and all expenditures audited be adopted?</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td><strong>YES</strong><br><strong>NO</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p><a href="https://files.santaclaracounty.gov/exjcpb1296/2026-08/measure_r_orchard-school-district-parcel-tax-primary-argument-in-favor_8.11.26_redacted.pdf?VersionId=KJFpM.O2H8XyU2WpuN8dF7X2zJmG1lPX" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="1e26dc13-92a1-4c1a-b932-3da4953497b4" data-entity-substitution="media" title="Measure_R_Orchard School District-Parcel Tax-Primary Argument in Favor_8.11.26_Redacted"><strong>Primary Argument In-Favor</strong></a>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Primary Argument Against</strong><em> (none filed)</em></p><p><a href="https://files.santaclaracounty.gov/exjcpb1296/2026-08/measure-r-orchard-school-district-parcel-tax-ia-redacted-20260818.pdf?VersionId=OxQ5w3LdKR5wiJMFVOX5sGPFd78K1LMo" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="f302e8cb-b95e-4b51-8a74-17665afd0efc" data-entity-substitution="media" title="Measure R - Orchard School District - Parcel Tax - IA Redacted - 20260818"><strong>Impartial Analysis</strong></a></p><hr><table class="align-table-left align-table-center"><caption><strong>El Camino Healthcare District</strong><br><strong>Measure S</strong><br><strong>Limit District Directors to Four Four-Year Terms</strong><br><strong>Majority Vote Required</strong></caption><tbody><tr><td>Shall the measure amending the Bylaws of the El Camino Healthcare District to limit District Directors to four four-year terms be adopted?</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td><strong>YES</strong><br><strong>NO</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p><a href="https://files.santaclaracounty.gov/exjcpb1296/2026-08/measure-s-el-camino-healthcare-district-echd-primary-argument-in-favor_redacted.pdf?VersionId=WMZ_ALjnrC.OXzcX4sTcqpOqQyuWXdhR" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="1b47821d-eca9-499a-b3b2-400be9ba615a" data-entity-substitution="media" title="Measure S - El Camino Healthcare District (ECHD) Primary Argument in Favor_Redacted"><strong>Primary Argument In-Favor</strong></a>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Primary Argument Against</strong><em> (none filed)</em></p><p><a href="https://files.santaclaracounty.gov/exjcpb1296/2026-08/measure-s-el-camino-healthcare-district-term-limit-ia-redacted-20260818.pdf?VersionId=xmPSrlttoIZIT1LZ.IX2_wKliVkdpmT3" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="99417adf-2009-4b87-9b09-1b13a1bf0deb" data-entity-substitution="media" title="Measure S - El Camino Healthcare District - Term Limit - IA Redacted - 20260818"><strong>Impartial Analysis</strong></a></p></div>
  
